    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d257">

                <pb facs="0491" n="429" sameAs="frus:frus1944Quebec/pg429"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">J.C.S.
                    Files</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the United States Chiefs of
                    Staff</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        C.C.S. 677/1</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Quebec</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1944-09-13">13 September 1944</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Future Operations in the
                        Mediterranean</hi></p>
                <p rendition="#flush">Reference: CCS 172d Meeting,
                    Item 5<hi rendition="#italic">c</hi>.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d257-f1"/></p>
                <p>The United States Chiefs of Staff have considered the draft message to General
                    Wilson proposed by the British Chiefs of Staff (Enclosure “A”) in connection
                    with item 5<hi rendition="#italic">c</hi>, C.C.S. 172d Meeting, and recommend <pb facs="0492" n="430"
                        xml:id="pg430"/> that the Combined Chiefs of Staff dispatch the message
                    attached as Enclosure “B” to SACMed in lieu
                    of Enclosure “A.”<anchor n="2" xml:id="d257-f2"/></p>



                <xi:include href="d257-a1.xml" xpointer="d257-a1"/>
                <xi:include href="d257-a2.xml" xpointer="d257-a2"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d257-f1" n="1" xml:id="d257-f1-content">
                <p>See <hi rendition="#italic">ante</hi>, <ref target="#pg305">p. 305</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d257-f2" n="2" xml:id="d257-f2-content">
                <p>At their 173d Meeting, September 13, 1944, the Combined Chiefs approved the
                    dispatch to Wilson of the message printed as enclosure “B”, below. See <hi
                        rendition="#italic">ante</hi>, <ref target="#pg322">p. 322</ref>. The
                    message was sent as telegram No. <hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">Fan</hi> 415.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
